# Sqlx embeds migration content at compile time and hashes the raw
# bytes. If Windows checkouts rewrite the files to CRLF while a
# Linux/macOS build leaves them LF (or vice-versa), the binary's
# embedded checksum diverges from whatever was stored in the user's
# `_sqlx_migrations` table on first apply, and every subsequent boot
# fails with "migration N was previously applied but has been
# modified". Forcing LF here makes the bytes deterministic across
# platforms.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
